+Owner skill: `skill://ts-conventions`. The merge-request page's pure core (plan §2 #128–#135, request `docs/slices/request-merge-requests.md` rules 3, 4, 5, 6, 8; design `.omp/run/notes/MrOverviewDesign.md` §2.1, §6 "B2 → B4 and B5"): the filters (any checked value within a filter, every filter across; "Me" is the logged-in user, never a username "me"; "None" an empty list; Draft all / drafts / ready), the checklists' choices (Me first when known, None, the others by name; Label None first; counts over the whole loaded list; a checked value not in the list kept, counted 0), the list's order (`merged`: one row per iid, the later copy wins, newest created first, ties by iid descending), the summary line, "created … ago" (the largest whole unit; a month is 30 days, a year 365), the CI box's contents (failed jobs, allowed-to-fail last; no job: the status in words) and the remembered form (`"me" | "none" | "user:<username>"`, `"none" | "label:<title>"`; junk reads as no filter).
+
+`index.ts` is the only surface. Framework-free (PM3) and self-contained: nothing here imports another `src/` module, as `search/` (PM2, `frontend/scripts/fences.ts`). Pure: no DOM, no timers, no storage, no state; the window's `ui/` owns loading, remembering (`ui/mergeRequestFilters.ts`) and the page's other words.
+
+`internal/`: `filters` (the filter types, `passes`, the edits, `filterLabel`), `choices`, `order`, `summary`, `relativeTime`, `ciBox`, `stored`. Every file has its `*.test.ts` (node), each test named for the bug it catches.
